  "live_records": {
    "q-120716": {
      "dom_id": "step-q120716",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=24{x}^{2}+20x+4$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $7.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 7 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(24{x}^{2}+20x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 7 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(8{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}+4x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 7 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(8{c}^{3}+10{c}^{2}+4c)-0] \\\\ 7 & =8{c}^{2}+10c+4 \\\\ 0 & =8{c}^{2}+10c-3 \\\\ 0 & =(2c+3)(4c-1) \\\\ c & =-\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=\\frac{1}{4}$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
