    "q-344715": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344715",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199393/assets/dfa665cf99f35e5cd2edef04b3f334f0054bbce7fc9b66c519d59d30e77ba2a1.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[0,10],$ is shown above. It consists of line segments.\n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[1,9].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,5].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [5,9].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
